<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Tangents: find k so that a line is a tangent (INNODEMS)</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>The line \( y = {@gl@} \) is a tangent to the curve</p>
\[ f(x) = x^2 - kx, \]
<p>where \( k \) is a constant. Suppose the line touches the curve at the point where \( x = a \). Two conditions must hold at \( x = a \): the <strong>gradients match</strong>, and the <strong>line and curve meet</strong>.</p>
<p>(a) Use the gradient condition \( f'(a) = {@mm@} \) to write \( k \) in terms of \( a \).</p>
<div>\( k = \) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]]</div>
<div>[[feedback:prt1]]</div>
<p>(b) Substitute your expression for \( k \) into the meeting condition \( f(a) = {@mm@}a - {@ss^2@} \). Find all possible values of \( a \).</p>
<div>\( a \in \) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]]</div>
<div>[[feedback:prt2]]</div>
<p>(c) Hence find all possible values of \( k \).</p>
<div>\( k \in \) [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]]</div>
<div>[[feedback:prt3]]</div>
<p>Enter the answers to (b) and (c) as sets, for example <code>{-1, 4}</code>.</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>(a) Gradient condition.</strong> \( f'(x) = 2x - k \), so at \( x = a \):</p>
\[ 2a - k = {@mm@} \quad\Longrightarrow\quad k = {@ta1@}. \]
<p><strong>(b) Meeting condition.</strong> The point \( (a,\ a^2 - ka) \) lies on the line, so \( a^2 - ka = {@mm*a + k0@} \). Substituting \( k = {@ta1@} \):</p>
\[
\begin{align*}
a^2 - ({@ta1@})a &= {@mm*a + k0@} \\
{@expand(a^2 - a*ta1)@} &= {@mm*a + k0@} \\
-a^2 &= {@k0@} \\
a^2 &= {@ss^2@},
\end{align*}
\]
<p>so \( a = {@ss@} \) or \( a = {@-ss@} \). Both square roots count.</p>
<p><strong>(c)</strong> From \( k = {@ta1@} \):</p>
\[ a = {@ss@} \Rightarrow k = 2({@ss@}) - ({@mm@}) = {@2*ss - mm@}, \qquad a = {@-ss@} \Rightarrow k = 2({@-ss@}) - ({@mm@}) = {@-2*ss - mm@}. \]
<p>So \( k \in {@ta3@} \): there are two different curves of the form \( y = x^2 - kx \) that the line touches.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
